<ul>
	<li>go to <samp><kbd>Settings</kbd> → <kbd>Reading</kbd></samp>, set the the <strong>Front page displays</strong> to <strong>a static page</strong> and select the front page and the blog page in the appropriate dropdowns,</li>
	<li>go to <samp><kbd>Appearance</kbd> → <kbd>Menus</kbd></samp>, select the main menu from the dropdown at the top and click on <strong>Select</strong>. Scroll to the bottom and set the <strong>Theme location</strong> to <strong>Main Menu</strong> (if there are more locations you can also assign other menus to those locations),</li>
	<li>go to <samp><kbd>Appearance</kbd> → <kbd>Widgets</kbd></samp>, and set <strong>Custom menu</strong> widgets, by selecting the correct menu (in <i>footer</i> and <i>our services</i> sidebars),</li>
	<li>optionally set other things (like logo, colors, ...). These settings can be found in <samp><kbd>Appearance</kbd> → <kbd>Customize</kbd></samp>.</li>
</ul>
